    "logic": {
      "concept": "Wang & Yang (2009): 30-minute energy futures show nonlinear directional predictability ONLY in bull states. Long-only by construction. A macro uptrend (Close > EMA(200)) and a trending tape (ADX(14) > 20.0) say the state is right; an autoregressive momentum trigger (this bar's return positive) with a functional-coefficient proxy Ut = Close - SMA(30) > 0 is the entry event; and the trade is confined to the NYMEX open-outcry window 09:00-14:30 ET, where the hedging flow the premise rests on actually transacts. The asymmetry is the fragile part of the premise and the 2023+ holdout is what settles it.",
      "entry": "LONG when Close > EMA(200) and ADX(14) > 20.0 and the bar stamp is inside [09:00, 14:30) ET, AND Close > Close[1] and Ut = Close - SMA(30) > 0, AND Volume > SMA(Volume, 20) and ATR(14)/Close > 0.0005. SHORT: never - the premise is bull-state only.",
      "exit": "Close crossing back BELOW SMA(30), the bracket at 2.0 x ATR(14) (trailing=False) or 3.0 x ATR(14) as a target, or the 14:30 ET session flatten - whichever the bar reaches first. Every exit is filled at the NEXT bar's open, so the flatten leaves at 15:00 ET."
    }
  },
